.\" Xrtg.1 -- userland/packages/x11r6.3.  MIT, see LICENSE in userland/packages.
.TH XRTG 1 "2026-11-15" "x11r63" "X11R6.3 on Amix"
.SH NAME
Xrtg, Xzz9000, X \- X11R6.3 server for RTG cards (the ZZ9000 and Z3660 RTG)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B Xrtg
[
.BI : display
] [
.I option
\&...
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Xrtg
is the X server for the RTG output of a graphics card under Amix: the
MNT ZZ9000, the Z3660 accelerator's RTG and the MNT VA2000.  It draws one
16-bit TrueColor screen into the card's framebuffer through the card's
driver
.RB ( /dev/zz9000 ,
.BR /dev/va2000 )
and uses the card's blitter for large fills and copies.  Keyboard and
mouse come from the Amix screen manager, as for the stock servers.
.PP
.B Xzz9000
and
.B X
are the same program.  The name it is started under picks the card:
.B Xzz9000
drives the ZZ9000/Z3660 card, as it always has;
.B Xrtg
and
.B X
take the first card the server finds.
.B \-card
overrides both.
.PP
The server needs the card driver loaded and must run as root: the
driver's node is readable and writable by root and group sys only.  Start it as root,
from
.BR xdm (1)
or from
.BR xinit (1)
and
.BR startx (1)
run by root.  It switches the monitor to the RTG output while it runs
and back to the Amiga video when it ends.
.PP
The keys Alt-Esc and Alt-F1 to Alt-F10 belong to the system, which uses
them to switch screens; X does not see them.  X keycodes are the Amiga
raw key codes plus 8 (8 to 135).
.SH OPTIONS
Besides the options every X server takes (see
.BR Xserver (1)),
.B Xrtg
takes these:
.TP 8
.BI \-card " name"
The card to drive:
.B zz9000
(the ZZ9000 or the Z3660 RTG),
.B va2000
(the VA2000), or
.B auto
for the first card the server finds.  A card this server has no driver
for stops it with a message.  The default is the card the server's name
says, else
.BR auto .
.TP 8
.BI \-mode " width" x height
The screen mode.  On the ZZ9000/Z3660: one of 640x480, 800x600,
1024x768, 1280x720, 1280x800, 1280x1024, 1920x800 and 1920x1080, as far
as the card offers it; the default is 1920x800.  On the VA2000: one of
640x480, 800x600, 1024x768, 1280x720, 1280x1024 and 1920x1080.
A mode the card does not have stops the server with the card's list.
.TP 8
.B \-audiobell
Ring the bell on
.B /dev/audio
(Paula).  The bell is off without this option: the stock audio driver's
open waits for Paula with interrupts blocked and no timeout, so on a
machine where Paula does not answer (an emulator with its sound output
off, a faulty chip) the first bell would freeze the whole machine.
.TP 8
.BI \-blitmin " pixels"
Fills and copies of at least this many pixels on the screen go to the
card's blitter; smaller ones, other raster operations and everything in
pixmaps are drawn by the CPU.  The default is the card's (1024 on the
ZZ9000/Z3660; 1024 on the VA2000, not yet measured on the card); 0 never
uses the blitter.  The server also stops using
the blitter, for the rest of its run, if the driver says the card or
mode has none.
.TP 8
.BI \-blitmax " pixels"
Accepted and ignored: the card driver splits every blitter operation
into bands itself.
.TP 8
.B \-move16
Copy images to the screen with the 68040/68060
.B move16
instruction.  Off by default; never on a 68030.
.TP 8
.B \-nomove16
Do not use
.BR move16 .
.TP 8
.BI \-ar1 " milliseconds"
.PD 0
.TP 8
.BI \-ar2 " milliseconds"
.PD
The delay before a held key repeats, and the time between repeats
(1 to 30000).  The X Keyboard Extension takes them; with
.B \-kb
(no X Keyboard Extension) the server repeats keys itself with these
times.
.B xset r
turns repeat off and on, for all keys or one.
.PP
The options
.BR \-mono ,
.BR \-zaphod ,
.BR \-heads ,
.BR \-spread_heads ,
.BR \-group ,
.BR \-type ,
.BR \-flags ,
.BR \-width ,
.BR \-height ,
.B \-depth
and
.B \-debug
belong to the Amix screen manager's native displays and are not for
use with the RTG screen.
.SH "EXTENSIONS"
MIT-SHM is not built: it would let any client have the server, which
runs as root, read or write any shared-memory segment on the machine.
Clients fall back to ordinary image requests.
.SH FILES
.TP 20
.B /dev/zz9000
the card driver (the z3660rtg package)
.TP 20
.B /dev/audio
the bell, with
.B \-audiobell
.TP 20
.B /etc/display.d
the server command line for each display type (the card's package
installs the one for its card)
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR Xserver (1),
.BR xdm (1),
.BR xinit (1),
.BR startx (1),
.BR xset (1),
.BR xmodmap (1)
